==Trivia==
*The word "Knight" comes from the German "Knecht", meaning servant or vassal. Originally, knights were associated with mounted warriors, later being considered a class of lower nobility, until eventually, knighthood had become associated with the ideals of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chivalry chivalry], a code of conduct for the perfect courtly Christian warrior. Often, a knight was a vassal who served as an elite fighter or a bodyguard for a lord, with payment in the form of land holdings.
**In the Chinese and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Mega Knight's name translates to "Super Knight". In the Italian and Arabic language settings of the game, the Mega Knight's name translates to "Great Knight" and "Giant Knight" respectively
*The Mega Knight’s Evolution was the first {{Rarity|Legendary}} [[Cards|card]] to receive a [[Card Evolution]].
*The Mega Knight is 1 of 2 evolved troops that has been featured under the [[Ruler Ability#Clash Melee|Clash Melee]] [[Ruler Ability|ruler ability]], the other being P.E.K.K.A.
*When the Evolved Mega Knight is defeated, his maces fall to the ground.
*Upon deployment, the Evolved Mega Knight yells “''Mega Knight!''”.
**The Mega Knight is 1 of 9 evolved troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Bomber/Evolution|Bomber]], [[Wizard/Evolution|Wizard]], [[Goblin Cage/Evolution|Goblin Brawler]], [[Witch/Evolution|Witch]], P.E.K.K.A., [[Hunter/Evolution|Hunter]], [[Executioner/Evolution|Executioner]], and [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack]].
***Also, the Mega Knight is 1 of 6 evolved troops whose regular troop do not speak distinct words when on the field, the others being Bomber, Goblin Brawler, Witch, Hunter, and Executioner.
*The Mega Knight’s Evolution is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
*In [[Touchdown]], the Evolved Mega Knight will push troops towards the center where the [[King's Tower|King Tower]] would be located, despite the lack of it.
*When an Evolved Mega Knight uppercuts a troop, that troop will stretch horizontally and take on a pink shade. This effect can stack up. Therefore, if multiple Evolved Mega Knights uppercut the same troop at the same time, the hit troop will become very stretched and pink while in the air.

